• The decoder’s boundary arithmetic is correct, including the `E0`, `ED`, `F0`, and `F4` second-byte restrictions and EOF offsets. One scope question remains: the new comment judgment treats bare CR as a terminator, so I’m checking whether that observable choice is recorded anywhere or is an extra rule beyond the cited `// … end of line` wording.

